{
  "about": "The washi tapes in the tray's Tape tab. Yours to edit: change colors, add your own, or delete any. A tape is a base color with layers of pattern on top, then a paper finish and a cut end. size is slim, regular or wide. edge is how the ends are cut: cut, zigzag, wavy, scallop or torn. base is a hex color. opacity (0 to 1) is how see-through the tape is. Each layer has a type (stripes, dots, gingham, checks, grid, hearts, sparkles, stars, daisies, leaves, stitch, waves, bunting, confetti, gradient, foil, film, rim, text), ink (a list of hex colors), and sometimes scale (how big one repeat is), size, angle, text, count or inset. Write {c0} to {c4} in any color to use that day's five palette colors. id is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, and a postcard remembers it, so avoid renaming one you have already used. The order here is the order in the tray; the five tapes made from the day's colors come last.",
